From c25d3031662ba70ec46ca022a2be7573f7293c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jul 2024 11:32:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1166/1695] drivers: scmi-msg: specific OSTLv4/v5
 duty-cycle/round_rate messages

SCMI clock protocol message IDs CLOCK_DUTY_CYCLE_GET and
CLOCK_ROUND_RATE_GET are specific to OSTLv4 and OSTLv5 and supported
only when the SCMI agent uses SMCI Clock protocol v1.0 or v2.0. This
is because they conflict with SCMI clock protocol v3.0 message IDs
CLOCK_CONFIG_GET and CLOCK_CONFIG_GET.

his change implements SCMI clock protocol v3.0 message IDs
CLOCK_CONFIG_SET (new message payload ABI) and CLOCK_CONFIG_GET
(to get the duty cycle of a clock). When using SCMI clock protocol
v3.0, the clock round rate request goes through CLOCK_DESCRIBE_RATES
messages.

This change makes the SCMI server to treat CLOCK_CONFIG_SET over SCMI
clock protocol v2.0 and OSTL legacy message IDs CLOCK_DUTY_CYCLE_GET
and CLOCK_ROUND_RATE_GET, using the payload size to distinguish between
these OSTL specific messages and the SCMI clock protocol v3.0 message
IDs CLOCK_ROUND_RATE_GET and CLOCK_POSSIBLE_PARENT_GET.

